Hi listfolk,

To follow-up on this, it seems Olivier found a bug in mrds (which does
the underlying work in the Distance package).

This bug effects binned (grouped) distance analysis when the half-normal
detection function is used only (bug has existed since at least
mid-2014). It effects only AIC comparison between that model and other
models, parameter estimates should be correct.

A patched version of the code is available on github and will be
included in the next release of Distance for Windows. Those wishing to
use the github version can follow instructions here:

https://github.com/DistanceDevelopment/mrds/wiki/LatestVersion

to update. Again, note this only effects analyses using grouped/binned
distances.

Thanks to Olivier for highlighting this issue and providing code to
assist in tracking it down.

cheers,
--dave

