This seems like a basic question that I may be overthinking. If I am standing at a point, surveying for birds, and one of my target species is perched at the top of a very tall tree, which distance do I measure: the distance to the bird at the top of the tree, or the distance to the tree itself, at eye level? On one hand I'm envisioning distance sampling involving two dimensions (thus I would measure to the tree at eye level), but everything I'm reading in the texts specifies that I should record the observer-to-organism distance. Thanks in advance.

Nick

